From: Yassin Rezai <yassinrsocial@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno: Match FD735 with any fuse id

The msm kernel driver reports the GPU speed bin in bits 47..32 of the
chip id and sets them to 0xffff when no fuse is read, so the A735 of
SM8635 (Palawan) shows up as 0xffff43030b00 and no device table entry
matches:

  MESA: error: fd_pipe_new2:49: unsupported GPU id 0x0 / chip id 0xffff43030b00

Use the wildcard fuse id like the Adreno X1-45 entry it shares its
configuration with. KGSL reports 0x43030b00, which still matches.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yassin Rezai <yassinrsocial@proton.me>
---
--- a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
+++ b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
@@ -1035,7 +1035,7 @@
 
 add_gpus([
         GPUId(chip_id=0xffff43030c00, name="Adreno X1-45"),
-        GPUId(chip_id=0x43030B00, name="FD735")
+        GPUId(chip_id=0xffff43030B00, name="FD735"),
     ], A6xxGPUInfo(
         CHIP.A7XX,
         [a7xx_base, a7xx_gen2, GPUProps(enable_tp_ubwc_flag_hint = True)],
